    title: "java (reproduced) + kotlin/ruby (shape): an extends/implements or super source is the run-wide class looked up by bare package-less name, so two same-named classes in different packages cross (WI-kosar family, outside lang-extended1)"  # cbb2
    status: todo_hard  # cbb2
    priority: 2  # cbb2
    parent:  # cbb2
    tags:  # cbb2
    - analysis_quality  # cbb2
    - call_resolution  # cbb2
    isbefore: []  # cbb2
    duplicate_of: []  # cbb2
    not_duplicate_of: []  # cbb2
    pr_ref:  # cbb2
    description: "Found by the WI-jusah sweep (2026-10-31), WI-kosar family, outside hypergumbo-lang-extended1 (which WI-jusah fixed for luau, apex, hack, smithy and prisma). Shape: the ENCLOSING/SOURCE symbol of an edge is fetched by bare (package-less) name from a run-wide, name-keyed table, so two files declaring the same name cross. LIVE rule: an enclosing symbol is found by the declaration's POSITION (core symbols_at / symbol_declared_by / enclosing_declared_symbol over file_symbols()).\n\nREPRODUCED (1): java.py ~L2689 and ~L2730, extends/implements emission in _extract_edges: src_sym = class_symbols[current_class], where class_symbols is the run-wide type table keyed by the dotted class name WITHOUT package (passed at ~L4221). Fixture: x/Base.java and y/Base.java (package x / y, each `public class Base`), a/Foo.java `package a; import x.Base; public class Foo extends Base` and b/Foo.java `package b; import y.Base;` (two blank lines) `public class Foo extends Base`. Output: BOTH extends edges have src a/Foo.java:3-7:Foo:class and dst x/Base.java (the line-5 edge is b/Foo.java's; it should be b.Foo -> y.Base). The base-class resolver (_resolve_base_class_java, WI-guvuz) then disambiguates against the WRONG class's file imports.\n\nSHAPE MATCHES, NOT REPRODUCED (read only):\n- java.py ~L4100 (inheritance pre-pass for global_class_parents): src_sym = class_symbols.get(current), same package-less key; and ~L4152: cls_sym = class_symbols.get(cls_name) attaches the global_class_fields meta to whichever same-named class registered last.\n- kotlin.py ~L1903 (INV-dupol super.m()): owner_sym = class_symbols.get(owner) with class_symbols built from global_symbols.values() (~L1700), so super.m() in one of two same-named classes walks the other's base_classes.\n- ruby.py ~L507 _superclass_of(class_name, global_symbols): the enclosing class's superclass read off the run-wide by-name symbol. Ruby reopens classes by name, so this may be intended; it needs a decision, not just a fix.\nLooked at and NOT members: solidity.py ~L194 (name fallback is a pragma'd dead path behind a span match), elixir.py ~L2129 (file table first; module names are app-global), jupyter.py ~L337 (per-notebook table, disambiguated by start line), cmake.py ~L310 (CMake target names are project-global), swift.py ~L2500 (base-type walk, a type resolution not an enclosing lookup). The two-file same-name fixture idea is already WI-gilur."  # cbb2
    fields: {}  # cbb2
- op: discuss  # aa8c
  at: '2026-11-01T04:45:51Z'  # aa8c
  by: agent  # aa8c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aa8c
  clock: 2  # aa8c
  nonce: aa8c  # aa8c
  message: "gikuk fix agent: commits d725063070 (java), 2067eef2f3 (kotlin), 4ee578222e (ruby) on branch jgstern-agent/fix/gikuk, unmerged; status left unchanged. All three shapes REPRODUCE, plus five more members in java.py / kotlin.py, all fixed on the branch:\n\nJAVA (reproduced as filed): both extends edges src a/Foo -> x/Base. Also reproduced: (1) pre-pass global_class_parents/global_class_fields keyed by package-less name -> b/Foo's inherited conn.commit() typed from x.Base (java.sql.Connection) instead of y.Base (java.io.File); y/Base meta.fields None, x/Base got the merge. (2) helper() / this.helper() / this::helper in b.Foo bound a.Foo.helper (run-wide name-keyed resolver). (3) _resolve_base_class_java had no same-package tier: package b; class Foo extends Base with a.Base and b.Base fell to the by-id pick (a.Base). (4) the Site-1 hand-off carried only the package-less enclosing_class name. Fix: source/owner by position (java's run-wide (path,line,col) index, the twin of core symbol_declared_by), parents/fields keyed by symbol id, own-class calls bind this file's member, enclosing_class_id stamped on hand-offs (WI-supat id path), same-package tier keyed by package-qualified name. End to end (run_behavior_map): b.Foo.m helper() -> a/Base.helper before, b/Base.helper after.\n\nKOTLIN (reproduced): super.m() owner by bare name -> b.Foo's super.m() reached p.BaseA.m; two outer classes' nested Inner in one file crossed; b.Bar (import y.Base) super.m() -> x.Base.m. Also this.m() / ::m / this::m bound another package's Foo.m, and same-package bases (no import) crossed in both extends and super. Fix (incl. a same-package tier, FileAnalysis.package): core enclosing_declared_symbol owner, _kt_import_target for the base member, same-package lookup, _own_class_lookup, same-package tier in _resolve_base_class_kotlin.\n\nRUBY (decision: it IS a member, changed). The bare class name drops module nesting: module A; class Foo < BaseA and module B; class Foo < BaseB both got BaseA as super's enclosing_class; a top-level Foo < Base leaked into B::Foo's super. Reopening is by FULL constant path (A::Foo), not bare name, so the fix keys the reopen fallback by qualified_name: the class by position (core enclosing_declared_symbol), its own superclass, else the superclass declared for the same qualified name anywhere in the run. Reopen in either file order still reaches the declared superclass (tests).\n\nResiduals NOT fixed: java super.m() still binds the class's OWN m (Case 1 treats super like this; pre-existing); java nested base by simple name (class L extends P where P is N.P) finds no candidate; kotlin this.m() the class does not declare keeps the run-wide name lookup (may still cross; kept for extension functions); kotlin super.m() through a same-package base that inherits m keeps the name lookup.\nCorpus A\\/B (analyze_java edge set): confluent-examples 31 removed \\/ 33 added (all removed cross-file; exercises\\/ copies of src\\/main services), killbill 22 \\/ 28 (catalog.MockProduct vs mock.MockProduct, MockPlan, TestEventJson); edges whose line lies outside their source span 2->0 and 6->0."  # aa8c
