- op: discuss  # 43dd
  at: '2026-11-01T07:56:27Z'  # 43dd
  by: agent  # 43dd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 43dd
  clock: 4  # 43dd
  nonce: 43dd  # 43dd
  message: "Fixed in PR #1985 (merged to dev 6afecacb1b). Root cause: the SOURCE of an extends/implements edge, the class whose fields/parents a call walks, and Kotlin/Ruby super's owner were fetched from run-wide tables keyed by the package-less class name, so two same-named classes in different packages crossed. Fix: every enclosing class is found by its declaration's POSITION. Java: _java_symbol_declared_by over a run-wide (path, line, col) index for extends/implements src, class_parents and class_fields keyed by id, own-class this.m(), a same-package tier for the base; _get_enclosing_method is now position-only, and its name fallback is deleted (it could only pick a twin). Kotlin: super.m()/this.m()/::m owner by position. Ruby: _superclass_of by position, plus the qualified name for a reopened class. 23 tests in 3 new files. Live repro on merged dev, the item's own fixture (x/Base, y/Base, a/Foo import x.Base, b/Foo import y.Base): `hypergumbo survey j1` rc=0 -> extends a/Foo.java:3-6:Foo -> x/Base.java (0.95, java); extends b/Foo.java:5-8:Foo -> y/Base.java (0.95, java). Before: both edges src a/Foo. Kotlin fixture (Foo in a.kt / b.kt, bases BaseA / BaseB): calls a.kt Foo.m -> bases.kt BaseA.m; b.kt Foo.m -> bases.kt BaseB.m. Ruby (A::Foo < BaseA, B::Foo < BaseB, each `super` in go): a.rb Foo#go -> BaseA go (meta enclosing_class BaseA); b.rb Foo#go -> BaseB go. Full suite on the integration branch: 37217 passed, 0 failed; check-package-coverage mainstream 100%. Residual, a DIFFERENT stage, filed separately: the core inheritance linker still adds b/Foo -> x/Base at conf 0.5, disambiguation_fallback=True, because its dedup is keyed by (src, dst) pair, not by base name. It predates this PR."  # 43dd
